@startuml
title OmniTrade AI - UML sequence from user input to explainable report
skinparam shadowing false
actor Analyst
participant "Web GUI" as GUI
participant "Public API" as API
participant "Workflow Runtime" as Runtime
participant "Evidence Service" as Evidence
participant "Model Gateway" as Model
participant "Report Service" as Report
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Event Stream" as Events

Analyst -> GUI : configure ticker, process, providers, models, policy, budgets
GUI -> API : createRun(configuration)
API -> API : authenticate, authorize, resolve published version
API -> Runtime : validate and execute immutable snapshot
Runtime -> DB : save run and initial state
Runtime -> Events : run.started
par five evidence roles
  Runtime -> Evidence : collect and normalize selected role
  Evidence --> Runtime : accepted evidence / disclosed degradation
else other evidence roles
  Runtime -> Evidence : collect and normalize selected role
  Evidence --> Runtime : accepted evidence / disclosed degradation
end
Runtime -> DB : checkpoint evidence states
Runtime -> Events : node events + checkpoint
par selected specialists
  Runtime -> Model : typed specialist request
  Model --> Runtime : schema-valid point of view
else other selected specialists
  Runtime -> Model : typed specialist request
  Model --> Runtime : schema-valid point of view
end
loop configured research depth (1..4)
  par opposing cases
    Runtime -> Model : bull case with cited evidence/counterpoints
    Model --> Runtime : typed bull case
  else
    Runtime -> Model : bear case with cited evidence/counterpoints
    Model --> Runtime : typed bear case
  end
end
par three risk attitudes
  Runtime -> Model : aggressive risk view
  Model --> Runtime : typed view
else
  Runtime -> Model : balanced risk view
  Model --> Runtime : typed view
else
  Runtime -> Model : conservative risk view
  Model --> Runtime : typed view
end
Runtime -> Runtime : apply profile limits and validate decision
Runtime -> Report : executed states + decision + evidence refs
Report -> DB : load evidence metadata and build claim lineage
Report -> Report : render JSON / HTML / PDF and hash artifacts
Report --> Runtime : report identity + lineage completeness
Runtime -> DB : save terminal state, report, artifacts
Runtime -> Events : run.completed or run.degraded
GUI -> API : reconnect events / get owned report and lineage
API --> GUI : live states + report + artifacts
GUI --> Analyst : explainable decision support (no order)
@enduml
